#: privacy.html:10
msgid ""
"Clementine is a music player that runs on your computer. It has no accounts,"
" analytics, advertising or tracking."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:11
msgid ""
"It connects to other computers only for the features you use, and this page "
"lists what it sends, and to whom."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:12
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Clementine Remote, the app for controlling Clementine from your phone, has "
"its own privacy policies for %(android)s and %(ios)s."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:14
msgid "Crash reports"
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:16
msgid ""
"The macOS and Windows builds, and the Debian, Ubuntu and Fedora packages, "
"published by the Clementine project can send a report to Clementine's "
"developers when Clementine crashes, so they can fix the problem."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:17
msgid "Packages made by Linux distributions themselves never send reports."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:18
msgid ""
"The next time Clementine starts after a crash, it asks whether to send the "
"report. Nothing is sent unless you agree, and you're asked again each time."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:19
msgid ""
"You can turn the question off in Preferences, under Behavior; turning it off"
" deletes reports that haven't been sent."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:21
msgid ""
"A report says what Clementine was doing when it crashed: the code it was "
"running and part of the memory it was using, the version of Clementine, and "
"the version of the operating system and the type of processor."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:22
msgid ""
"Because it includes some of Clementine's memory, it can include file names, "
"which can include your user name, and the titles of songs you were playing."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:23
msgid ""
"Reports are sent to Sentry, which stores them for us in the EU, without the "
"IP address they were sent from, and deletes them after at most 90 days."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:24
msgid ""
"They are used only to fix crashes, and only Clementine's developers can see "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:26
msgid "Updates"
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:28
msgid ""
"On macOS, Clementine asks whether it may check for updates automatically."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:29
msgid ""
"Checking downloads a list of releases from data.clementine-player.org, which"
" sees which version of Clementine you have."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:30
msgid ""
"On Windows you can download new releases from this website, and on Linux "
"your distribution's package manager updates Clementine."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:32
msgid "Clementine's own services"
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:34
msgid ""
"Some features use services the Clementine project runs at data.clementine-"
"player.org:"
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:37
msgid ""
"The artist information pane sends the name of the artist that's playing, and"
" your language, to fetch a biography and photos. Our server looks them up "
"with Google and Spotify on your behalf, so those services see only the "
"artist's name, and keeps the answers for a while so it doesn't have to ask "
"again."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:38
msgid ""
"Signing in to Box or Dropbox returns to Clementine through our server, which"
" passes a one-time sign-in code back to Clementine on your computer. "
"Clementine then signs in with the service directly, and the code can't be "
"used again."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:39
msgid ""
"The Rainy Mood background stream and the Icecast radio directory are opened "
"through our server, which counts how many times each is used, without "
"recording who used it."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:42
msgid ""
"These services run on Google Cloud, which keeps a log of the requests made "
"to them, including the IP address they came from, for 30 days. We use the "
"logs only to keep the services running."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:44
msgid "Services you choose to use"
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:46
msgid ""
"Clementine sends requests straight to other services when you use the "
"features that need them. Each sees your IP address and what Clementine asks "
"it, and handles them under its own privacy policy:"
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:49
msgid ""
"Last.fm: the songs you play, if you sign in to Last.fm and turn on "
"scrobbling, and the song that's playing, when the song information pane "
"shows information about it."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:50
msgid ""
"Last.fm, MusicBrainz, the Cover Art Archive and Discogs, when you look for "
"album covers: the artist and album."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:51
msgid ""
"LRCLIB, when the song information pane shows lyrics: the song's title, "
"artist, album and length."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:52
msgid ""
"AcoustID and MusicBrainz, when you ask Clementine to complete a song's tags:"
" an audio fingerprint of the song, and the tags it finds."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:53
msgid ""
"Internet radio, music and podcast services, such as SomaFM, Radio Browser, "
"Jamendo, Magnatune, DI.fm and gpodder.net: what you browse, search for and "
"play."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:54
msgid ""
"Cloud storage and music servers you connect, such as Google Drive, Dropbox, "
"OneDrive, Box, Seafile, Subsonic and Plex: the requests for your music "
"there."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:57
msgid ""
"The user names, passwords and sign-in tokens you give Clementine for these "
"services are kept in Clementine's settings on your computer, and are sent "
"only to the service they belong to."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:59
msgid "Your local network"
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:61
msgid ""
"Clementine finds AirPlay and Sonos speakers on your local network, and sends"
" music only to the ones you choose."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:62
msgid ""
"If you turn on the network remote, Clementine Remote on your phone can "
"control it, browse your library and download songs from it."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:63
msgid "This all stays on your local network."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:65
msgid "This website"
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:67
msgid ""
"This website has no analytics, advertising or cookies. It runs on Google "
"Cloud, which keeps a log of the pages requested, including the IP address "
"they came from, for 30 days."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:68
msgid "Pages in Burmese load a font from Google Fonts."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:69
msgid "Downloads come from GitHub, which has its own privacy policy."
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:71
msgid "More information"
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:74
msgid "Clementine's source code, where you can check all of this"
msgstr ""

#: privacy.html:75
msgid "Questions: open an issue on GitHub"
msgstr ""
